<main>
    <section class="pl-hero fade-up fade-up-2">
        <div class="pl-left">
            <h1>Your AI tools don't share what they know about you.</h1>
            <p class="pl-label">Why it exists</p>
            <ul class="pl-problem-list">
                <li>Claude Code, Claude Chat, ChatGPT, Gemini — each starts from scratch, siloed from the others</li>
                <li>Inside each tool, memory is one flat pile instead of organized by project and context</li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="pl-right">
            <p class="pl-product-name">Parachute Vault <span class="alpha-tag">alpha</span></p>
            <p class="pl-desc">A self-hosted knowledge graph that lives on your machine. Every AI you use reads and writes to the same graph over <a href="https://modelcontextprotocol.io" target="_blank">MCP</a> — notes, tags, links, project context. One source of truth you and your AIs share.</p>
            <p class="pl-desc">Extensible. Open source. Your data, your hardware.</p>

            <p class="pl-label">Get started</p>
            <div class="code-inline">
                <code>bun add -g @openparachute/cli &amp;&amp; parachute install vault</code>
            </div>
            <p class="pl-install-note">Requires <a href="https://bun.sh" target="_blank">Bun</a>. Run inside any Claude Code session — Vault is picked up automatically.</p>
            <a href="https://github.com/ParachuteComputer/parachute-vault" class="pl-cta-btn" target="_blank">View Parachute Vault on GitHub</a>
            <div class="pl-secondary-links">
                <a href="/install/">Full install guide &rarr;</a>
                <a href="/blog/">Blog &rarr;</a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="pl-grid fade-up fade-up-3">
        <div class="pl-cell">
            <h2>How it connects your AIs</h2>
            <p>Run <code>parachute expose public</code> and your Vault lands at a stable HTTPS URL. Point Claude (web / Desktop / mobile), ChatGPT, Gemini, or any MCP-capable tool at the same URL. They all read and write to the same graph.</p>
            <p>Notes written in one session appear in the next. Project context follows you across tools, not just sessions.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pl-cell">
            <h2>The graph compounds over time</h2>
            <p>Wikilinks resolve, tags accrete, notes point at each other. As your AIs read and write, context gets richer — organized by project, linked by topic, queryable as a whole.</p>
            <p>Everything is a SQLite file on your disk. Your data is yours, portable, and doesn't require us to exist.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pl-cell">
            <h2>Simple primitives, open surface area</h2>
            <p>Everything flows through a small MCP tool set. Your AI calls these; your own scripts, apps, and services call the same ones — AI and traditional software building on the same foundation.</p>
            <div class="pl-tool-chips">
                <span class="pl-tool-chip">query-notes</span>
                <span class="pl-tool-chip">create-note</span>
                <span class="pl-tool-chip">update-note</span>
                <span class="pl-tool-chip">list-tags</span>
                <span class="pl-tool-chip">find-path</span>
                <span class="pl-tool-chip">vault-info</span>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="pl-cell">
            <h2>Auth-gated by default</h2>
            <p>OAuth 2.1 + TOTP for human clients. Scoped API tokens for scripts and agents. Every endpoint requires proof — the <code>parachute expose</code> path is about making your Vault <em>reachable</em>, not about removing the gate.</p>
            <p><a href="/install/#claude-chat">Set up for claude.ai / ChatGPT &rarr;</a></p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <div class="pl-aside fade-up fade-up-4">
        <strong>Want a UI for your notes?</strong> We've built <a href="https://github.com/ParachuteComputer/parachute-notes" target="_blank">Parachute Notes</a> — an alpha PWA that talks to your Vault. Install with <code>parachute install notes</code>, or fork it and build your own. It's an example of what any developer can build on the open API.
    </div>

    <section class="pl-principles fade-up fade-up-5">
        <h2>Principles</h2>
        <div class="pl-principles-grid">
            <div class="pl-principle">
                <strong>Local-first</strong>
                <span>SQLite on your disk. Nothing in the cloud unless you ask.</span>
            </div>
            <div class="pl-principle">
                <strong>Open standard</strong>
                <span>Built on <a href="https://modelcontextprotocol.io" target="_blank">MCP</a>. Any AI today or next year.</span>
            </div>
            <div class="pl-principle">
                <strong>Open source, AGPL</strong>
                <span>Read every line of code that touches your notes.</span>
            </div>
            <div class="pl-principle">
                <strong>Extensible</strong>
                <span>Small, stable service contracts. Plug in your own modules.</span>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
</main>
